                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "caf3f05f-16e9-303c-bf9a-6a07800e4ffa",
                        "entry_id": "978fecbc-9c5b-3e5c-a983-adf29aa21fa3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "мед. нарушение деятельности органа, системы органов или всего организма в целом вследствие неспособности их приспособительных механизмов компенсировать вызванные болезнью нарушения"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef93beb4-036a-4a23-90fb-413a8c7bb6c3",
                                "sense_id": "caf3f05f-16e9-303c-bf9a-6a07800e4ffa",
                                "text": "Лактатный ацидоз — прямое следствие и раннее проявление начинающейся декомпенсации гипоксии, предшествующее тяжелым нарушениям биоэнергетики клетки."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3c6c5325-f8e3-408c-90b4-6e75ed2909e2",
                        "source_entry_id": "978fecbc-9c5b-3e5c-a983-adf29aa21fa3",
                        "source_sense_id": "caf3f05f-16e9-303c-bf9a-6a07800e4ffa",
                        "target_lang_word": "decompensation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "decompensation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4831c9d-a328-3c34-93b0-affb1605b9c3",
                                        "entry_id": "4897418a-97ec-3d57-9827-de78f9b152ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The inability of a diseased or weakened organic system or organ to compensate for its deficiency, resulting in functional deterioration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af1db7b3-13ac-4c63-87c4-f93b65ecb292",
                                                "sense_id": "e4831c9d-a328-3c34-93b0-affb1605b9c3",
                                                "text": "Once it was determined that hyperthyroidism was the probable etiology of her cardiac decompensation, the next step was treatment of the underlying disease."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9bcf67e4-5c15-3e9c-a6f7-f507ded06fcf",
                                        "entry_id": "4897418a-97ec-3d57-9827-de78f9b152ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The deterioration of cognitive or emotional functionality in a person who is distressed or who suffers from a psychological disorder."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a747b0c-5280-43ac-b81f-e3e3cc246165",
                                                "sense_id": "9bcf67e4-5c15-3e9c-a6f7-f507ded06fcf",
                                                "text": "A varying percentage of our combat soldiers reach the limit of their endurance and must leave their foxholes, not for physical wounds but because of emotional decompensation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
